From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:52:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: uapi: h264: add stateless MVC decoding controls

Add what a stateless decoder needs to decode H.264 Multiview Video
Coding (Annex H; the Stereo High and Multiview High profiles) on top of
the existing H.264 controls:

- V4L2_CID_STATELESS_H264_MVC_VIEWS: a dynamic array with one element per
  view of the active subset SPS, in view order index order: its view_id
  and its anchor and non-anchor inter-view references per list, as
  seq_parameter_set_mvc_extension() gives them. Drivers advertise the
  number of views they can decode as the maximum number of elements. The
  default (one element, all zero) is a stream without MVC.
- V4L2_CID_STATELESS_H264_MVC_DECODE_PARAMS: the view order index of the
  view component a request decodes, and its anchor_pic_flag and
  inter_view_flag from nal_unit_header_mvc_extension().
- struct v4l2_h264_dpb_entry gets the view order index of the entry, out
  of its reserved bytes (the layout and the size do not change), and the
  V4L2_H264_DPB_ENTRY_FLAG_INTER_VIEW flag for the inter-view references:
  the pictures of the other views of the same access unit that the view
  component predicts from.

Each view component is decoded by a request of its own, the base view
first, with the slices of that view only: NAL units 1/5 for the base
view, 20 for the other ones. The DPB holds the references of the view
being decoded and its inter-view references; drivers which build the
initial reference lists append the inter-view references after the
temporal ones (H.8.2.1).

The controls take the IDs at the stateless codec base + 9 and + 10 and
the control types 0x0207 and 0x0208.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
